# Proton VPN preset.
#
# Config source: account.protonvpn.com -> Downloads -> WireGuard configuration.
# Each generated config carries its OWN keypair and counts as one session.
#
# Quirks that matter here:
#   * In-tunnel resolver is 10.2.0.1 and speaks PLAIN DNS only. If you run
#     DNS-over-TLS globally in strict mode, you must disable DoT on the VPN
#     link or all name resolution breaks while connected. the importer does
#     this automatically (connection.dns-over-tls no).
#   * Peer sections carry a server comment like "# SE#21", which the importer
#     turns into the profile name proton-se-21.
#   * One session per key. Reusing a config in two places kills both tunnels.

PROFILE_PREFIX="proton"
FALLBACK_DNS="10.2.0.1"

# Regex that extracts a server tag from the config's peer comment.
SERVER_TAG_REGEX='^#[[:space:]]*[A-Z]{2}(-[A-Z0-9]+)*#[0-9]+'

# Proton's in-tunnel resolver does not support DNS-over-TLS.
LINK_DNS_OVER_TLS="no"
